      "message": "As a follow-on you could auto-generated these case statements with a macro.\n\nSomething like:\n```\n#define BBRAM_REGION_PROPERTIES(child_id, offset, size) \\\n    case UTIL_CAT(SYSTEM_BBRAM_IDX_, \\\n                  DT_STRING_UPPER_TOKEN(child_id, region)): \\\n        *offset \u003d DT_PROP(child_id, offset); \\\n        *size \u003d DT_PROP(child_id, size); \\\n        break;\n                  \nswitch (idx) {\n    DT_FOREACH_CHILD_VARGS(DT_PATH(named_bbram_regions), BBRAM_REGION_PROPERTIES, offset_out, size_out)\n    default:\n        return EC_ERROR_INVAL;\n}\n```\n\nThis would require adding an enum property to the named-bbram-regions called \"region\".  This improves the BBRAM region driver, as it no longer relies on the node names to identify the region.",
